Chapter: Saturate

 Saturating arithmetic for bounded contexts. Each operation clamps
 its result to the given [lo, hi] range instead of overflowing.
 Every function is punctual: no heap, no recursion, bounded
 instruction count.

 We say:

Section: General Saturating Arithmetic

  punctual sat-add : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sat-add (lo) (hi) (a) (b) =
    let r = a + b
    in if r < lo then lo else if r > hi then hi else r

  punctual sat-sub : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sat-sub (lo) (hi) (a) (b) =
    let r = a - b
    in if r < lo then lo else if r > hi then hi else r

  punctual sat-mul : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sat-mul (lo) (hi) (a) (b) =
    let r = a * b
    in if r < lo then lo else if r > hi then hi else r

Section: Byte-Width Saturating Arithmetic

  punctual sat-add-u8 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sat-add-u8 (a) (b) =
    let r = a + b
    in if r > 255 then 255 else if r < 0 then 0 else r

  punctual sat-sub-u8 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sat-sub-u8 (a) (b) =
    let r = a - b
    in if r < 0 then 0 else r

  punctual sat-add-u16 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sat-add-u16 (a) (b) =
    let r = a + b
    in if r > 65535 then 65535 else if r < 0 then 0 else r

  punctual sat-sub-u16 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sat-sub-u16 (a) (b) =
    let r = a - b
    in if r < 0 then 0 else r

